{
 "name": "bike-hook",
 "description": "Garage wall hook that hangs a bike by its top tube, the bike parallel to the wall. Inferred: up to 15 kg (most road and mountain bikes, not e-bikes), held for ten years (creep), 1.5x its weight when lifted on or off, about once a day for ten years; a sideways knock at half the weight; top tube up to 50 mm, centred 165 mm out so the handlebars and pedals clear the wall; two #10 (M5) wood screws in a vertical line into one stud. PA 12 (MJF): the bike hangs for years and is lifted on and off daily, so the hook needs a nylon with measured fatigue and creep data and no weak layer direction; PETG's layer bond failed that first.",
